  "answer_text": "Great question \u2014 and honestly, there's no single \"correct\" answer, but here's a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## How to Pronounce \"Doge\" \ud83d\udc15\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, \"doge\" can be pronounced **three** main ways: **/do\u028a\u0292/**, **/do\u028ad\u0292/**, or **/do\u028a\u0261/**. Here's what each sounds like in plain English:\n\n---\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfc6 **\"Dohj\"** \u2014 *Most widely accepted* (rhymes with \"rouge\")\n**IPA: /do\u028a\u0292/**\n\nThe pronunciation \"dohj\" (written as /do\u028a\u0292/ in IPA) was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*. In one of the episodes, a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj.\"\n\nLanguage columnist Ben Zimmer stated, \"In deference to Strong Bad, I would favor /do\u028a\u0292/ or /do\u028ad\u0292/ (with the J sound).\"\n\n---\n\n### 2. **\"Dohg\"** \u2014 *Like \"vogue\" but with a D* (rhymes with \"rogue\")\n**IPA: /do\u028a\u0261/**\n\nSome people argue that since the original word is \"dog,\" which has a hard G, the E only modifies the vowel \u2014 sort of like how \"slop\" becomes \"slope\" and \"mop\" becomes \"mope.\" So \"dog\" becomes \"doge,\" pronounced like \"rogue.\"\n\n---\n\n### 3. **\"Doh-geh\"** \u2014 *Two syllables, like \"doggy\" with an accent*\n**IPA: /do\u028a\u0261e\u026a/**\n\nThis pronunciation features a long O, hard G, and spoken \"e\" sound like at the end of \"ballet,\" and is preferred by some because it sounds like a bastardized version of \"doggy.\"\n\n---\n\n### 4. **\"Dog\"** or **\"Doggy\"**\nSome people just say it like the animal. These people exist too. Let us speak no more of them. \ud83d\ude04\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddd0 The Verdict\n\nSince \"Doge\" is a word that was practically made up for the purposes of an internet meme, it's no surprise that there's a lot of confusion. But **\"dohj\"** (rhyming with *rouge*) is the most widely used pronunciation in media and the one confirmed by the creators of Dogecoin, so that's your safest bet.\n\nMuch pronunciation. Very debate. Wow. \ud83d\udc36",
